    "forensics": "The recent losses stem from two distinct microstructure regimes: mid-morning (10:25) liquidity traps in INFY and TATASTEEL where our 0.65% stop loss was slightly too tight to absorb normal post-open consolidation volatility, and late-session (13:45-14:10) stagnation where signals lacked the time and volume expansion to reach the ambitious 1.45% target before the EOD square-off. In the afternoon trades, minuscule gross movements resulted in net losses purely due to transaction fee drag consuming over 60% of gross profits across the cycle.",
